Z||000000||WisconsinGT||10-23-2000||11:25 PM||||I have been listening to this for a couple of weeks now. It sounds like a faint intermittent grumble only when I am at a stop light. I do not hear it when the car is in motion. Anyone have any idea what could be going on? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Vlad||10-24-2000||02:06 AM||||Hard drive ????????      :-))<P>There is nothing moving in ECM. Probably that noise comes from different place?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-24-2000||07:15 AM||||Check you heat shield attachments, some may be loose. Also check bell housing covers for loose or missing bolts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||10-24-2000||08:29 AM||||I don't think it's the ECM, nothing whirls around in it.<P>I agree with resto guy, check the heat shields in the engine compartment.  There's one just below the rear window and one down underneath the car just ahead of the starter.  Also the rock shield on the catalytic converter is prone to rust out and makes everything all grumbly.  Hope this helps...<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||10-24-2000||10:47 AM||||I've had circuit boards buzz, chirp, whistle, pop, and squeal, but not grumble.  Maybe a bearing in an alternator.  Low RPM grumble out of that?  Fuel pump??? The gas guage should freak out if it's a fuel pump.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-24-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000005||curtis||10-24-2000||09:43 PM||||Mine does the same thing and Its the material <BR>breaking up and moving around in my cat very. About to replace it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mbramble||10-24-2000||10:12 PM||||I had the same sound.  Only noticed it when I was stopped at a light or something.  I thought it was coming from the rear speakers.  A couple days ago I found  3-4 holes in my cat.  After patching them up I noticed that the noise is gone.  Maybe the sound coming from those holes was of a frequency that was causing the rear window to resonate???  Don't know, but the feint rumbling noise is now gone....<BR>||||reg||1
